From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Callaghan <johnocallaghan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:25:10 +0100
Subject: media: meson: vdec: do not fail poll() while OUTPUT streams

The parser consumes OUTPUT buffers at once.
H.264, VP9 and HEVC start the CAPTURE queue later, after the source
change event. In that window v4l2_m2m_poll() returns EPOLLERR.

GStreamer then fails to start about one time in two.
FFmpeg loops on POLLERR.

Ignore the error while the OUTPUT queue streams without errors.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-sonnet-5-5
Signed-off-by: John O'Callaghan <johnocallaghan@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c | 23 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c
@@ -960,12 +960,33 @@ static int vdec_close(struct file *file)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The ESPARSER consumes the OUTPUT buffers as soon as they are queued, so the
+ * OUTPUT queue is usually empty, and codecs with dynamic resolution support
+ * (H.264, VP9) only start the CAPTURE queue after the source change event.
+ * v4l2_m2m_poll() takes that for a stalled session and returns EPOLLERR,
+ * although events and decoded buffers are still going to arrive. Whether
+ * userspace polls in that window is a race, so don't report an error as long
+ * as the OUTPUT queue is streaming without errors.
+ */
+static __poll_t vdec_poll(struct file *file, struct poll_table_struct *wait)
+{
+	struct amvdec_session *sess = file_to_amvdec_session(file);
+	struct vb2_queue *src_q = v4l2_m2m_get_src_vq(sess->m2m_ctx);
+	__poll_t rc = v4l2_m2m_fop_poll(file, wait);
+
+	if ((rc & EPOLLERR) && vb2_is_streaming(src_q) && !src_q->error)
+		rc &= ~EPOLLERR;
+
+	return rc;
+}
+
 static const struct v4l2_file_operations vdec_fops = {
 	.owner = THIS_MODULE,
 	.open = vdec_open,
 	.release = vdec_close,
 	.unlocked_ioctl = video_ioctl2,
-	.poll = v4l2_m2m_fop_poll,
+	.poll = vdec_poll,
 	.mmap = v4l2_m2m_fop_mmap,
 };
 
